<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-4568] IPython&apos;s clear_output doesn&apos;t work in Zeppelin</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-4568</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;That means user can not refresh the interpret result via clear_output&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; sys
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; time
from IPython.display &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; display, clear_output
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; i in range(10):
    time.sleep(0.25)
    clear_output(wait=True)
    print(i)
    sys.stdout.flush()
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
